Z||000000||KRMFiero||03-14-2001||11:25 AM||||I just got my Idle Air Control Valve in from The Fiero Store. I took the old on out (car had a idle of 2000-3000 RPM until it warmed up) now with the new one it idle's at 3000-4000 rpm (AHHHH!, I'm not waiting to see if it goes down when it warms up)    What should I do?  Whats wrong?  HELP ME!!!     <P>The new one also looks not as long? does it contract or something?<P>Kyle<P>Btw: I also ordered a power window switch for L/H side, now my window goes down   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (Red)<BR>1985 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (White)<P>      <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/sig2.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by KRMFiero (edited 03-14-2001).]||||reg||1
